# A handler that breaks the response protocol must cost one request a 500,
# never the worker (docs/compiler/server.md §15, "Never panic in Rust on
# input"; §3, "a worker whose isolate died answers 503"). Two workers serve
# this fixture, so the requests below alternate between them.

### a handler that returns undefined is a 500
GET /undefined
>>> 500

### a handler that returns a string is a 500
GET /not-an-object
>>> 500

### a thrown non-Error is a 500 without its text
GET /throw-string
>>> 500
!~ SECRET-DETAIL

### a rejected promise is a 500 without its message
GET /reject
>>> 500
!~ SECRET-DETAIL

### the workers still answer after every broken handler above
GET /alive
>>> 200
= still alive

### and on the other worker too
GET /alive
>>> 200
= still alive

### a third request is answered too
GET /alive
>>> 200
= still alive
